{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/994792-tremere-2e","id":994792,"title":"Tremere 2e","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-10-28T13:40:13-07:00","id":994792,"title":"Tremere 2e","content":"I've been giving some thought for how to make the Tremere a Bloodline, and I've come up with some stuff. This is assuming a world where magic-users exist, but they aren't quite Awakened, but it isn't a necessity since nothing I have is particularly dependent on Mage existing or not existing. <br /> <br /> So, they're a universal Bloodline, but Mekhet and Ventrue are the most likely to enter in. My idea for Gift is that they can potentially learn any mortal sorcery, Theban Sorcery, or Cruac spell regardless of Covenant (they still have to pay the merit cost, though, and they can't take on minor templates, use psychic powers, or perform sorcery that requires a patron or power source without access to that patron or power source), and they have a series of Devotions related to magic. Sensing it, defending against it, etc. <br /> <br /> Their weaknesses are the one from Masquerade, and I'm also thinking they either need to consume human souls or commit diablerie to use their powers, and because of this they're widely hated and distrusted, meaning most Tremere have to keep their Bloodline hidden. <br /> <br /> Their gift sounds kind of overpowered, but I'm trying to balance it out. For one thing, they still need to shell out experience points for their spells. They have a very wide menu of things they can learn, but they don't have any more merit dots to spend than any other vampire. And then there's their weakness. The original Masquerade weakness was kind of infamous for not being that big of a drawback, and a lot of STs made up for it by emphasizing the restrictive, conspiratorial nature of the clan and how no one else liked them. I kind of codified that with the &quot;widely hated and feared&quot; thing, and I also added soul eating to tie them to Mage's Tremere, which helpfully gives them yet another drawback, and one that provides a good reason why other vampires don't trust them. It isn't just &quot;they're jealous of their power&quot; or &quot;they're weirdos&quot;, it's that very few Princes are going to want a vampire that has to eat souls running around their city.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-28T13:48:35-07:00","id":994801,"title":"","content":"Not necessarily suggesting that Tremere should be Ordo Dracul by default, but if you look up the Coil of Zirnirtra in the <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1_J83T-t9g-87pvtUTKCZIJ2QQzCTOzUclkWJjsvb814/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Ordo Dracul playtest file</a> for Secrets of the Covenants, you may find something useful.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-28T13:53:36-07:00","id":994806,"title":"","content":"I've seen that one, and I'm keeping this kind of separate. There's enough of a thematic divide between &quot;blood sorcery&quot; and &quot;performing experimental surgery on yourself to give yourself psychic powers&quot; that I'd keep them as two different things. Plus, part of what I hope is keeping them from being too overpowered is that they can't really be a part of any Covenant unless they keep their bloodline a secret. <br /> <br /> And then there's the EXP issue- a Tremere who does join the Order and learns Zirnitra and starts learning supernatural merits isn't going to have many dots left over to learn much sorcery.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-28T14:19:04-07:00","id":994832,"title":"","content":"Couldn't a bloodline or clan of sorta Tremere come from a strix using synthesis on a mage they possessed ? I'm pretty intrigued by that power's potential for that, plus it'd be rare enough for that stuff to happen.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7104-s-brechen","name":"S. Brechen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-28T14:25:43-07:00","id":994839,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/994792-tremere-2e?p=994806#post994806\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've seen that one, and I'm keeping this kind of separate. There's enough of a thematic divide between &quot;blood sorcery&quot; and &quot;performing experimental surgery on yourself to give yourself psychic powers&quot; that I'd keep them as two different things. Plus, part of what I hope is keeping them from being too overpowered is that they can't really be a part of any Covenant unless they keep their bloodline a secret.<br /> <br /> And then there's the EXP issue- a Tremere who does join the Order and learns Zirnitra and starts learning supernatural merits isn't going to have many dots left over to learn much sorcery.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was more suggesting it as possible inspiration than actual use.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-28T15:41:26-07:00","id":994903,"title":"","content":"I did a writeup of them a little while back for 2e. A bit different than what you had in mind, because they have their own magic (based on Mage spells) and they are their own clan/bloodline combination, but maybe it'll provide some inspiration of some sort for you! If not, no worries, I know it's a little different.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1-vI88bjgHoXUa5_0qLKQIdMMMKknoUhvFCLzSY7nrOE/edit#heading=h.ojuw2xgzjocs\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1-vI88bjgHoXUa5_0qLKQIdMMMKknoUhvFCLzSY7nrOE/edit#heading=h.ojuw2xgzjocs\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1-vI88bjgHoXUa5_0qLKQIdMMMKknoUhvFCLzSY7nrOE/edit#heading=h.ojuw2xgzjocs\" target=\"_blank\"> https://docs.google.com/document/d/1-vI88bjgHoXUa5_0qLKQIdMMMKknoUhvFCLzSY7nrOE/edit#heading=h.ojuw2xgzjocs </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-28T19:20:15-07:00","id":995008,"title":"","content":"I think I'd still go with mine, but that doesn't mean that yours isn't really interesting and well done!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-29T08:56:03-07:00","id":995224,"title":"","content":"I won't talk too much here, because it isn't intended to stop your work and fun, but I personally wouldn't make the old Tremere into a Bloodline or Clan. Even at Masquerade I always thought they worked better as a cabal or conspiracy of scholarly vampires studying the arcane arts than as a clan. More like how the Sons of Osiris worked.<br /> <br /> So, to me at least, the Covenant structure is quite perfect for them. They could be something like a branch of the Ordo Dracul, or an insular Covenant of their own, with their own kind of Ritual Blood Magic, maybe ripped out of the two religious Covenants, and/or even from other magical traditions the world around.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-29T13:57:43-07:00","id":995330,"title":"","content":"Well, they're as much a conspiracy as a Bloodline. The way I've written up their place in Kindred society they're pretty much separate from the covenants, and they have their own organization and laws.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-29T14:56:36-07:00","id":995364,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/994792-tremere-2e?p=995330#post995330\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, they're as much a conspiracy as a Bloodline. The way I've written up their place in Kindred society they're pretty much separate from the covenants, and they have their own organization and laws.</div> </div> </div> </div>They have their own organization and laws?<br /> Isn't that kinda the definition of a covenant?<br /> <br /> Perhaps the blood tie ritual from old Masquerade blocks of the ability to join a bloodline, but allows them to learn their blood sorcery.<br /> <br /> The Blood tie could act in place of a bloodline weakness. <br /> <br /> Just a thought.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1117-overload","name":"overload","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1117_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"97"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-30T13:29:49-07:00","id":995782,"title":"","content":"As <b>overload</b> said. If they have their own society, then they are a Covenant by definition. Even if one of their requisites for membership is to be of the very same bloodline.<br /> <br /> That's the beauty of the 2nd Ed Covenants instead of the old Sects. They do the same, but with far more flexibility. They are social institutions for vampires, of any nature, each its own thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-01T12:05:33-07:00","id":996732,"title":"","content":"As something worth pointing out, the OP has shown a penchant for getting super-tied to terms and ideas that are, to put it as nicely as possible, not supported by the game lines. Do please note that it makes no nevermind to me that <b><a href=\"http://Geckopirateship\" target=\"_blank\">Geckopirateship</a></b>'s status is 'banned'... But that said, I don't find a Tremere bloodline as useful in the game as House of Tremere as a Covenant that contrasts \u2013 and necessarily pushes to the fore \u2013 an apparent contradiction within the Ordo Dracul. That is, I'd offer up a Tremere Covenant as mystics who use (mechanically) similar tools as the more scientifically-minded Dragons.<br /> <br /> In my version, the Ordo Dracul are built on ancient notions that Dracula didn't so much <i>INVENT</i> as he codified and made useful to the Kindred as a means of transcending their common curse \u2013 something supported to varying degrees within came 'canon'. Around the time of Vlad's Embrace, another group of Kindred used those same principles as the departure point for exploring the latent powers hidden in the Vitae for more personal use. Whereas the Defiant seek to push the boundaries of the un-dead experience for purposes of becoming MORE that mere Kindred, these Tremere use similar applications to make themselves the GREATEST of Kindred. It's a fine point, I concede, but I see it as the former being scientists who dabble in the occult, whilst the latter are mystics who sometimes use rational study to reach their goals. For me, it removes that 'squishy' tension between the study elements (e.g. experiments, defining Coils and Scales, the veneration of Prince Vlad's own explorations) and the mystical seeking for Dragon Nests and 'magical' thinking (especially as found in the <i>Ordo Dracul</i> book). So, why the Tremere?<br /> <br /> First, as they were presented in old <b>Vampire: the Masquerade</b>, their strict hierarchy forces them to work as a group, even as they are by nature a bunch of self-serving power grubbing wanks. Maybe they keep that pyramid imagery or instead fancy themselves a 'Black Academie', but as a group of Kindred seeking personal power, such a structure is vital to keep something like peace \u2013 not to mention is fair well oozes with conspiracy theory seeds when one considers the how and why of such structures. Second, the Tremere 'paradigm' has built-in nomenclature for their works; that is, their versions of the Mysteries are called Paths, their Coils are called Ways (hat tip to <b>Masquerade</b> Koldunic Sorcery), and their Scales are instead Sendings. Mechanically their 'Thaumaturgy' looks like the Rites of the Dragon 'with the serial numbers scratched off', but its Paths are based more on elemental and fundamental themes \u2013 think primal sources of power akin more to elemental <i>EFFECTS</i> like volcanoes and floods than to the 'classical' elements themselves \u2013 that come across in allegorical forms rather than objective, 'throw a fireball' sort of expressions. Magic IS an art to them! It's Dracula's followers who wanna be scientists. Needless to say, these Tremere see the pursuit of POWER as their only core belief, leading them to regard the Sanctified and Acolytes \u2013 who practise 'lesser magics' of faith \u2013 as fledgling babes afraid to leave a safe nest of empty promises.<br /> <br /> ...I dunno if any of this makes sense to anyone else, but it's my take. I have written a lot about this version of the House of Tremere Covenant, but my troupe has scattered since <b>Vampire: the Requiem</b> Second Edition came out, meaning there's been no playtest or even serious discussion on the idea so far. It's a very 'niche' viewpoint, too, I know. That notwithstanding, I very much like the portrayal of Dracula-as-scientific-thinker in the game, but his bouts with mysticism as shown in <i>Rites of the Dragon</i> felt at odds with this. I mean, I didn't want <b>Mage: the Awakening</b> to be the ONLY line in this game milieu to have Tremere!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>B.I.G. Bird spreads the word: Anybody with a heart votes love<br /> <a href=\"https://absintheandthorns.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">https://absintheandthorns.obsidianportal.com/</a></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/409-phaolan","name":"Phaolan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar409_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"478"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-01T16:19:47-07:00","id":996870,"title":"","content":"I actually liked this take of yours, <b>Phaolan</b>, though I would add some notes.<br /> <br /> The mysticism mixed in the Dragons' work doesn't bother me because it clearly isn't such a clear distinction in setting. The &quot;hermetic mysticism&quot; is one of the first expressions of the naturalistic philosophy that created modern science, it was a natural side-effect of a scientific thinking alongside a superstitious thinking, that by its side is a natural development of the human brain, specially among too many unexplained phenomena. Such things still exist a lot today IRL, in a setting with so many mysteries it is even more likely. But at the core, the Dragons are still scientific-minded to a great degree.<br /> <br /> About the Tremere themselves, I think there is, in fact, a lot of inspiration that can be taken from the cWoD history of Clan Tremere, including their previous time as House Tremere. Another take that could be used could be a link between this House Tremere and the Awakened, to some degree.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-01T19:10:25-07:00","id":996939,"title":"","content":"When I want to translate my Tremere characters from Masquerade to Requiem I usually make them members of the Ordo Dracul or The Circle of the Crone, am personally not a fan of Bloodlines so...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12561-shawarbaaz","name":"Shawarbaaz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12561_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"467"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-02T02:18:39-07:00","id":997056,"title":"","content":"In my game, I've added a Tremere covenant which also has an associated bloodline (as suggested in the Vampire Translation Guide). I'm fine with bloodlines as long as there aren't too many of them running around.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-02T08:36:38-07:00","id":997158,"title":"","content":"I have no problem with bloodlines when they make sense, though I barely use them myself.<br /> <br /> But the Tremere work wonderfully as a Covenant. IMHO they should be that way since Masquerade.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-02T11:48:52-07:00","id":997284,"title":"","content":"And that's why they're a covenant in my game. They just also happen to be a bloodline that makes up a significant minority of the covenant.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}